WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.888 --> 00:00:03.550
- (screams) It's so fluffy, oh my God!

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.740
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.130
Hey guys I'm Brenda,
I'm a tasty producer

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:13.020
and today we will be comparing American

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.690
versus Japanese cheesecakes.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.930
Now I'll be taking care of the classic

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.300
creamy cheesecake that you
guys all know really well.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.880
- And I'm Alvin, and I'll be making

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.640
the jiggly Japanese cheesecake
because I think it's such a

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.010
unique twist on cheesecake that you

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.960
probably seen online and it's so cool.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.940
I'm gonna show you exactly how it's done.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.690
- Okay let's start this
American cheesecake.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.630
So to make the base, you
get your graham crackers,

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.310
and you smash until they turn into this.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.670
The reason why I begin
with the crust is that

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.420
it has to be baked twice.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:47.550
Once by itself, and then
with the cheesecake mix.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.620
So while this is baking,
you can just go ahead

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.090
and get started with your cheesecake mix.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.810
I'm not gonna run all
my ingredients at once.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.760
What I'm actually doing is starting

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.680
with the sugar and the cream cheese.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.640
I also have all my ingredients
at room temperature.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.070
All of this will make it
easier to avoid lumps,

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.090
and will help me combine
everything perfectly.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.620
Let's go back in time to this
recipe Alvin filled before,

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.990
which happens to inspire my recipe.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.310
Look at the way it comes in.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:26.380
The texture that it appears
to have, it's just beautiful.

00:01:29.638 --> 00:01:32.221
(upbeat music)

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.830
- Let's cook this Japanese cheesecake.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.890
So the process is very different

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:43.400
than a traditional cheesecake,

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.300
this starts with making a
liquid cheesecake mixture

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.350
of cream cheese, milk, butter and sugar.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.680
And once that gets all nice and smooth,

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.830
that gets folded into egg yolks

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.600
and that becomes this sort of like creamy,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.910
liquidish kind of batter,

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.850
and that sort of your cheesecake base.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.670
When I went to Japan to work
with the Taste of Japan team,

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.070
we had our eyes set on
this jiggly cheesecake

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.660
that had been like a
viral trender on there

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.780
for a really long time.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.580
It was just as amazing as it looked.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.090
It's a very light, fluffy, soft cheesecake

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.050
that's very airy, it's like a cloud.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.980
So it's like almost
you're making a meringue,

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.070
and then you sort of fold the meringue

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.870
back in to that cheesecake batter.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.150
The funny thing is that you
could eat the entire cheesecake

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.810
because 80% of this is air.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.540
When we were in Japan, it
was not uncommon to see

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.770
someone buying a whole
cheesecake for themselves

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.850
and finishing it on their walk to work.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.380
You need to bake it in a water bath.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.770
So what that does, it creates
like a nice steam barrier

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:45.690
around the cake, so the
cake will never get too hot

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.210
because the water will take
excess heat away from it.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.860
- [Brenda] This is one of
my favorite parts Alvin

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.960
because you're pretty much
unveiling this mythical creature.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.600
It looks super impressive,

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.270
you know it's gonna be very fluffy.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.800
- [Alvin] You know those
Tempurpedic commercials,

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.820
this is like memory foam for my hand.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.243
(upbeat music)

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.010
- Let's taste it.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.310
- Let's do it.
- Alright.

00:03:16.658 --> 00:03:19.740
- This cake right here,
is creamy, and it melts,

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:20.930
it's not too dense.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.210
- Your cheesecake, at least in my opinion,

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.720
in terms of texture is superb.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.110
This thing is super fluffy.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.650
Which one's your winner and why.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.280
- It will probably be the Japanese one.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.070
When I want something in a dessert,

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.060
I want something that isn't too heavy

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.530
so I can take more than one bite.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.170
- I'm gonna go for the Japanese version.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.110
Yes, this is easier to make,

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.340
but it seems a little more adventurous

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.920
to go for this one, and the
texture, the fluffiness,

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.890
and the jiggling is just
like out of this world.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.190
In a taste test, one out of three,

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.750
said that they would
go for your cheesecake.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.730
I asked people on Instagram, right there.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.280
69% on yours.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.460
- 31% on this one so.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.293
- There you go.

00:04:01.293 --> 00:04:02.800
- The crowd and the internet have spoken.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.050
Brenda, that's raw egg.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.670
- [Brenda] It's still delicious.

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:14.626
(jazz music)

